# A suspended Fabry-Perot cavity: the end mirror hangs on a pendulum.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for the model. Finesse.jl parses all of
# it and solves the frequency response. OpticalModelingToolkit.jl reads the
# subset it supports (see src/katscript.jl) and simulates the same network in
# the time domain.
#
#     l1 ── m1 ══ s0 ══ ══ sc ══ m2 ── (pendulum sus on m2.mech)

laser l1 P=50
mirror m1 R=0.99 T=0.01 L=0
mirror m2 R=0.999 T=0.001 L=0 phi=0
space s0 l1.p1 m1.p1 L=1
space sc m1.p2 m2.p2 L=0.1
pendulum sus m2.mech mass=0.1 fz=20 Qz=2
